      "postID": "59df684cf3d09b6f1c77ed70",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "Also, \"deputizing\" users to be mods globally is unlikely. At least in the near term. It takes a certain personality type and skill set to manage things properly. It could also be abused. It also has some potential legal issues for us since they'd not be employees of VRChat. At some point \"deputizing\" users in your instance or authored world should be possible allowing the creator/author and deputized users to kick or ban from those instances or authored worlds. I have another idea that I want to think through first before discussing that I think will help in a lot of ways. More on that later.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
